ntativeness":0.9462360739707947,"text_excerpt":"I love that a little food court shop has pretty authentic Viet food. Great place to stop for lunch when you just want a quick, filling bite to eat. We ended up here because I started craving non-salad vegetables after eating at so many places in NOLA with just (yummy) carbs and meat. We had both the Hainan chicken and steak, which were decent (The steak was a bit chewy for me; chicken was very tender). I really loved that they had a brown rice option for no extra charge. The vermicelli noodles were great. We also tried the grilled pork in a bao, and I wish I ordered the grilled pork for my entree. It's really well seasoned and super tender."},{"business_id":"43cADIQXfG3hDwuvLT78rg","review_id":"mD5K1HJEMxh-98nS962gcQ","date":"2018-03-27T09:26:10","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9097191691398621,"text_excerpt":"This Vietnamese fast food place is located inside a mall. My mom & I are Vietnamese. We are pretty picky when it comes to Vietnamese food. I actually enjoy their Pho Beef Noodle Soup. My 3 year boy likes their egg roll. My mom likes her rice dish. White rice with lemongrass chicken and stir fried cabbages. We both had Vietnamese ice coffee. We would definitely eat here again."},{"business_id":"43cADIQXfG3hDwuvLT78rg","review_id":"LGCqr1f9N8aX4v0cuCBMyQ","date":"2014-03-19T20:03:00","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9084108471870422,"text_excerpt":"i think that this is a great place and some of the better Vietnamese food in the city. It is in the food court on the second floor, and there is always a line. The staff is friendly and we always have a good meal."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
